<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Władysław II the Exile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1105–<a href="/years/1159">1159</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piast dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Władysław II the Exile was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-iii-wrymouth">Bolesław III Wrymouth</a> and, under his father's testament of 1138, High Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and Duke of Silesia. His attempt to dispossess his younger half-brothers failed, and in 1146 they drove him into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, where he died in 1159. With imperial backing his sons recovered Silesia in 1163, founding the Silesian line of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piasts</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-ii-the-exile.jpg" alt="Władysław II the Exile" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Matejko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wladyslaw_II_Wygnaniec_(76842400)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The first senior duke, <b>Wladyslaw II the Exile</b>, tried to rule alone and was driven out by his brothers in 1146.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-krakow">Duchy of Krakow</a></li><li><blockquote>After the partition of the Polish realm, Silesia was held by the sons of <b>Władysław II the Exile</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-opole-and-raciborz">Duchy of Opole and Racibórz</a></li><li><blockquote>By the testament of Bolesław III Wrymouth in 1138, Poland was divided among his sons, and Silesia, with its capital at Wrocław, went to the eldest, <b>Władysław II the Exile</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-silesia">Duchy of Silesia</a></li></ul></section>
